\par\par \b \uc2 Peru Stock Indexes Tumble To End Sharply Lower; Sol Unchanged\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Oktober 2008\par 21:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Emerging Markets Report\par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended sharply lower on Monday, continuing the slide that hit the market hard last week.\par \par \uc2 A decline on Wall Street and concerns about weaker-than-expected corporate earnings hurt the Lima bourse, especially blue chip shares.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's general index decreased 5.33% to end at 6,038.66.\par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip fell 6.57% to finish at 9,360.27.\par \par \uc2 The general index is now well down from its July 24, 2007, high of 23,789.75, while the selective index is down from its high of 42,139.76 on the same day.\par \par \uc2 Financial holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP) tumbled 9.59% to end at $31.01.\par \par \uc2 The company, which owns Peru's largest bank, Banco de Credito, is now well down from its 52-week high of $86.91.\par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (PCU) was down 3.20% at $10.30, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) ended off 8.33% at $7.59.\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell $93 million.\par \par \uc2 The sol ended unchanged, at PEN3.108 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to smooth out volatility.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-211 2652; peru@dowjones.com [ 27-10-08 2034GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument EM00000020081027e4ar0000t\par }\page {\par\