\par\par \b \uc2 Peru Stock Indexes End Sharply Higher On Metals; Sol Stronger\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2008\par 22:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended sharply higher Tuesday, with a boost from rising metal prices.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange's general index increased 5.46% to end at 9,141.01.\par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip rose 6.76% to finish at 15,079.78.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange is heavily weighted toward mining companies, as Peru is one of the world's biggest producers of base and precious metals.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, the mining subindex increased by 6.43%. Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) rose 15% at end at $15.24 on strength in copper prices. Zinc miner \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA (VOLB.VL) increased 12.6% to end at 1.88 soles ($0.62) in heavy trade.\par \par \uc2 Financial holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP) ended up 5.2% at $47.01. Credicorp owns Banco de Credito, \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's largest bank.\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell $48 million. With the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol ended slightly stronger, at PEN3.041 to the dollar compared with PEN3.042 the previous session.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to smooth out volatility.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-211 2652; peru@dowjones.com [ 10-14-08 1636ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020081014e4ae00053\par }