\par\par \b \uc2 Peru Stock Indexes End Sharply Lower; Sol Strengthens\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Oktober 2008\par 22:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended sharply lower Thursday, dragged down by weakness on Wall Street and in the mining sector.\par \par \uc2 The Lima Stock Exchange was also playing catch-up with other stock markets that had declined the previous day, when the Lima exchange was closed for a national holiday.\par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, Lima Stock Exchange's general index dropped 8.77% to end at 8,549.43.\par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index slid 9.08% to finish at 14,001.07.\par \par \uc2 The general index is now well down from its July 24, 2007, high of 23,789.75, while the selective index is down from its high of 42,139.76 on the same day.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the mining subindex fell by 9.72%.\par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (PCU) fell 13% to end at $11.31, while fellow copper miner, Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA,(CVERDEC1.VL) lost 11% to end at $13.80.\par \par \uc2 Financial holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP) ended down 2.7% at $44.77. Credicorp owns Banco de Credito, Peru's largest bank.\par \par \uc2 Telefonica SA\uc2  (TEF) slid 13.7% to end at $59.00, following the direction of its New York-traded American Depositary Receipt.\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell $280.5 million.\par \par \uc2 With the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol ended slightly stronger, at PEN3.080 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at PEN3.114 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to smooth out volatility.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  also placed 2.5 billion soles ($812 million) worth of one-week repurchase agreements, aiming to increase liquidity in the market.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-211-2652; peru@dowjones.com [ 10-09-08 1650ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020081009e4a90004t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
