\par\par \b \uc2 Peru Stock Indexes End Slightly Lower; Sol Weakens\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Oktober 2008\par 23:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes closed slightly weaker Friday, dragged down by some key blue-chip shares.\par \par \uc2 The stock market started the trading session with gains but then weakened after the U.S. Congress approved a $700 billion financial rescue bill.\par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index declined 0.09% to end at 10,777.90.\par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index fell 0.02% to finish at 18,028.65.\par \par \uc2 Financial holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP) ended down 3.5% at $55.00. Credicorp owns Banco de Credito, Peru's largest bank.\par \par \uc2 Copper miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (PCU) fell 1.3% to $15.60, while tin miner Minsur SAA (MINSURI1.VL) lost 1.8% to end at 5.35 soles ($1.78).\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell $99 million.\par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol ended slightly weaker, at PEN3.008 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at PEN3.004 to the dollar. The sol moved into the PEN3.0 to the dollar range for the first time this year on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Consulting firm Macroconsult said in a report that the sol has been weakening in recent trading sessions as investors withdraw holdings from emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 On Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed 1.0 billion soles ($332 million) in three-day repurchase agreements, and another PEN1.0 billion in two-day repos, adding liquidity to the market.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-211 2652; peru@dowjones.com [ 10-03-08 1708ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020081003e4a30004n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
