\par\par \b \uc2 Peru Stock Indexes End Higher On Blue Chips; Sol Weakens\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2008\par 22:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes closed stronger Wednesday, led by gains in various blue chip shares.\par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index rose 0.34% to end at 11,286.37.\par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip increased 0.72% to finish at 19,085.84.\par \par \uc2 Financial holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP) rose 1.6% to end at $60.40. Credicorp owns Banco de Credito, Peru's largest bank.\par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) gained 3.1% to end at 72.55 soles ($24.29) on improved metals prices.\par \par \uc2 Zinc miner \uc2 Volcan Compania Minera\uc2  SAA (VOLB.VL) rose 3.5% to end at PEN2.38 in heavy trade.\par \par \uc2 Going the other way was \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 . (PCU), which fell 4.6% to close at $18.41 on weakness in copper prices.\par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly weaker, at PEN2.9860 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at PEN2.9830 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  said in a report that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a record $2 billion in the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  spot market in September with the aim of reducing the volatility of the nominal exchange rate, and to prevent a depreciation of the nominal exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 "We think that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not want a sharp depreciation of the Sol because it could increase inflationary pressures and, potentially, it could reverse the recent de-dollarization of the financial system," it said.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-211 2652; peru@dowjones.com [ 01-10-08 2042GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020081001e4a1000ud\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
