\par\par \b \uc2 Peru cenbank works to keep Sol stronger than 3/dlr\b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2008\par 21:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LIMA, Sept 30 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market again on Tuesday in what traders said was a move to keep the sol firmer than 3 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which for much of this year was buying dollars to prevent a surging sol <PEN=PE> from overshooting, has since June been selling dollars from its $35 billion in international reserves. Reserves hit a record this year thanks to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar purchases.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $9 million on Tuesday at a preliminary rate of 2.9834, pulling the sol back slightly as it moved close to 3 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 On Monday, it made a much larger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of $418.6 million as global markets plunged after a $700 billion financial bailout package failed to win a key U.S. congressional vote.\par \par \uc2 Officials of Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have said they want to prevent excessive volatility in the sol, which could drive up inflation during a weakening cycle, or hurt exporters in a strengthening cycle.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly raised interest rates and tightened monetary policy this year in a bid to tame inflation, which has topped 6 percent over the last 12 months -- well above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of 2 percent, plus or minus a tolerance band of one percentage point.\par \par \uc2 During 2008, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold $2.3 billion and bought $8.7 billion on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. (Reporting by Jean Luis Arce, Writing by Terry Wade; Editing by Diane Craft)\par \par \uc2 PERU-ECONOMY/SOL|LANGEN|ABN|D|M|E|RBN|U|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080930e49u001nb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
