\par\par \b \uc2 Peru Stks End With Sharp Declines; Genl Index -2.13%; Sol Down\b0\par\par\uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 September 2008\par 22:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Of/ DOW JONES NEWSWIRES\par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended sharply lower Thursday, dragged down by weakness on Wall Street and declining metal prices.\par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index fell 2.13% to end at 12,952.25. The selective blue-chip index decreased 2.46% to finish at 21,619.37. The mining subindex lost 2.44%.\par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) continued to slide, dropping 8.2% to end at 57.00 soles ($19.20) on weakness in gold prices.\par \par \uc2 Financial holding company \uc2 Credicorp Ltd\uc2 . (BAP) fell 2.3% to end at $69.30.\par \par \uc2 Copper miner \uc2 Southern Copper Corp\uc2 .(PCU) declined 7.0% to end at $22.70 as copper prices eased.\par \par \uc2 The sol weakened slightly on Thursday, ending at PEN2.9680 to the U.S. dollar, compared with the previous session's PEN2.9650.\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell $253 million.\par \par \uc2 That follows \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell $70 million on Wednesday, which marked the first U.S. dollar sales by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  since July 1.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be concerned that a stronger dollar could lead to greater imported inflation pressures in Peru.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the sol has appreciated 1.03% against the dollar. Over the last 12 months, the sol has appreciated 6.14% against its U.S. counterpart.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-211 2652; peru@dowjones.com [ 09-04-08 1632ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837 5077   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020080904e4940004l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
