\par\par \b \uc2 Peru Stock Indexes End Lower; Sol Weakens Again\b0\par\par\uc2 287 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2008\par 22:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended sharply lower Tuesday, dragged down by weakness in the mining sector.\par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index fell 0.99% to end at 16,558.18.\par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index decreased 0.74% to finish at 27,352.70.\par \par \uc2 The mining subindex fell 1.3%.\par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2 (PCU) declined 2% to end at $110 on falling copper prices.\par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA(CVERDEC1.VL) lost 0.4% to end at $25.80.\par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) dropped 1.4% to end at 5.83 soles ($1.97) as zinc prices also fell.\par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to sell $80 million at an average of PEN2.9610 to the U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell $14 million in the previous session - the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars in 2 1/2 years, according to reports.\par \par \uc2 The sol ended weaker Tuesday, at PEN2.9630 to the dollar, after it ended the previous session at PEN2.9430.\par \par \uc2 Economists say the dollar has been strengthening in recent sessions as foreign investors withdraw their investments in instruments denominated in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and convert the funds into dollars.\par \par \uc2 The withdrawals are tied to higher reserve requirements set out by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 So far this year the sol has appreciated 1.20% against the dollar. Over the last 12 months, the sol has appreciated 6.53% against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-211 2652; peru@dowjones.com [ 06-24-08 1638ET ]\par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020080624e46o0009c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
