\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-IMF says Peru outlook good after loan review\b0\par\par\uc2 312 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Mai 2008\par 17:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (Adds context, quote, changes dateline, previous WASHINGTON)\par \par \uc2  LIMA, May 14 (Reuters) - Economic prospects in Peru are "favorable" despite inflation that has risen above the official target and pressures from a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the International Monetary Fund said on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2  An IMF team just completed its third review of a $278 million standby loan agreement that Peru signed in January of last year. The pact lasts for 25 months and the IMF's board is expected to vote on the outcome of the review by July.\par \par \uc2  The IMF praised officials for recent policy adjustments.\par \par \uc2  "The policy response has been prudent, including the announcement of a higher fiscal target for 2008 and the tightening of monetary policy," the IMF said after talks with Peruvian authorities. "The mission is encouraged by the authorities' firm commitment to maintaining macroeconomic stability."\par \par \uc2  Inflation, as measured by the price index of metropolitan Lima, has swelled 2.32 percent so far this year. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's annual inflation target is 2 percent, plus or minus one percentage point. Last year, inflation hit nearly 4 percent.\par \par \uc2  This year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been raising interest rates and deposit requirements in an effort to try to ease inflation.\par \par \uc2  It also has spent some $9 billion in 2008 \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stem the climb of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol, which has sharply rallied against the dollar over the last 12 months.\par \par \uc2  Peru's economy, one of the fastest growing in the world, expanded some 9 percent last year. In April, it won investment-grade status from rating agency Fitch and is expected to be upgraded by Standard and Poor's soon.  (Reporting by Lesley Wroughton in Washington and Dana Ford in Lima; Editing by Diane Craft)   \par \par \uc2 PERU-ECONOMY/IMF (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|ABN|M|D   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020080517e45e000d7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
