\par\par \b \uc2 Peru Stock Indexes End Sharply Higher; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 22:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended sharply higher Thursday, as stronger metals prices again helped lift mining company shares.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index increased 486.18 points, or 2.87%, to end at 17,431.85.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index rose 1,109.10 points, or 3.98%, to finish at 28,996.34.   \par \par \uc2 The mining subindex gained 3.85% in the session.   \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) rose 1.0% to end at 206.00 soles ($74.92).   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) gained 1.9% at end at $26.25 as copper prices improved.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) increased 5.0% to end at PEN8.35 as zinc prices rose.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $366 million at an average of PEN2.7507 to the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol ended stronger, at PEN2.7500 to the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at PEN2.7720 to the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Banco de Credito, in a report released before the market closed, said that \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far this year have been five times higher than those registered in the same period a year earlier.   \par \par \uc2 It noted that recent interest in the sol has come not only from local businesses seeking soles for tax payment