\par\par \b \uc2 Peru Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Strengthens A Bit   \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2008\par 22:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended higher Monday, as rising base metal prices lifted various mining company shares.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index increased 86.77 points, or 0.49%, to end at 17,853.71.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index rose 156.55 points, or 0.54%, to finish at 29,291.21.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) rose 0.7% at end at $27.20 as copper prices gained.   \par \par \uc2 Tin miner Minsur SAA (MINSURI1.VL) gained 0.6% to end at 8.10 soles ($2.81) on a rise in tin prices.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) increased 2.3% to end at PEN8.37 as zinc prices improved.   \par \par \uc2 The Lima stock market increased despite a decline on Wall Street.   \par \par \uc2 "It is to be expected that the Peruvian stock market will continue to disconnect from the movements of the stock markets in the United States in as much as the perspectives for growth in the Peruvian market remain strong and aren't expected to be impacted by a slowing U.S. economy," Banco de Credito said in a report.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended Monday slightly stronger at a midrate of PEN2.8845 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN2.8840-PEN2.8850.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN2.8895 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.8890-PEN2.8900.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $80 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $230 million.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say that there is expected to be strong demand for soles in March due to an annual income tax payment period.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 03-03-08 1647ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020080303e4330008d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
