\par\par \b \uc2 Peru Stock Indexes End Sharply Higher; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 275 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Februar 2008\par 22:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended sharply higher Wednesday, lifted by surging mineral prices that gave a boost to mining company shares.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index rose 440.99 points, or 2.54%, to end at 17,778.16.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index rose 899.26 points, or 3.20%, to 29,040.58.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) advanced 3.0% to finish at $115.82 on stronger copper prices, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) rose 2.0% to $27.10.   \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) gained 3.0% to end at 209.00 soles ($72.32) on stronger gold prices.   \par \par \uc2 The gain in Buenaventura's shares came about despite a strike at some of the company's mines in Peru by workers demanding greater profit-sharing.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLCABC1.VL) rose 7.3% to PEN8.05 on improved zinc prices.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly stronger at a midrate of PEN2.8935 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.8930-PEN2.8940.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN2.8940 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.8930-PEN2.8950.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $136.5 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent trading sessions, as various companies obtain soles for tax payment purposes.   \par