\par\par \b \uc2 Peru Stock Indexes End With Gains; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 238 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Februar 2008\par 22:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended higher Tuesday, lifted by rising blue chip shares.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index increased 308.18 points, or 1.81%, to end at 17,337.17.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index rose 720.44 points, or 2.63%, to finish at 28,141.32.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) rose 0.7% to end at $75.50 on improved interest in the banking sector.   \par \par \uc2 Tin miner Minsur SAA (MINSURI1.VL) continued to gain as tin prices hit a new record high. Minsur increased 2.4% to end at 7.68 soles ($2.64).   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) rose 4.9% to end at PEN7.50 in heavy trade.   \par \par \uc2 The sol continued to strengthen, ending at a midrate of PEN2.8940 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.8930-PEN2.8950.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN2.8970 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.8960-PEN2.8980.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $97 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly in recent trading sessions, as various companies obtain soles for tax payment purposes.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 02-26-08 1629ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020080226e42q000aw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\pic