\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  VIEW: Peru  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Moves Cool Hot Flows Into Sol   \b0\par\par\uc2 719 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Februar 2008\par 21:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \par \uc2 A Dow Jones Newswires Column   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Recent measures implemented by the Central Reserve Bank of Peru have successfully eased speculative pressures on the Peruvian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the sol.   \par \par \uc2 Last month, the sol faced heavy buying from both foreign and local investors, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to adjust how it reacts to smooth out volatility.   \par \par \uc2 "I think that the effects of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures are starting to be felt," said Jorge Gonzalez Izquierdo, an economist with the Universidad del Pacifico. Speculative flows into the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  "have fallen off substantially," he added.   \par \par \uc2 Speaking to a Congressional commission on Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Julio Velarde said the market has stabilized after what he called "massive" inflows of speculative capital in January. "In the last few days the market has been quiet, but it (volatility) could return again next week. We don't know," Velarde told Congress, according to newspaper Gestion.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Regularly   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows both the sol and the U.S. dollar as legal tender, and while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  says the sol is a free floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it does \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  when needed to avoid volatility.   \par \par \uc2 The sol has been steadily gaining against the greenback - it appreciated 7.0% against U.S. dollar last year and some 6.4% in 2006, boosted by a number of factors, including strong economic fundamentals, and robust exports.   \par \par \uc2 But the appreciation pressures took off at the start of this year as the interest rate spread between the U.S. and Peru appeared to be set to widen even more.   \par \par \uc2 As the sol began to appreciate - it gained 2.1% in January - domestic exporters concerned that the sol was gaining too much began to criticize government policies.   \par \par \uc2 Still, the Peruvian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased its reference rate 25 basis points in January to 5.25%, concerned about the possibility of rising inflationary pressures.   \par \par \uc2 Perspectives that the sol would appreciate even more led investors to chase the Peruvian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sharply increase purchases of government sol-denominated certificates of deposit.   \par \par \uc2 Average capital inflows were some $500 million a day in the first half of January, overwhelming a market more used to dealing with volumes closer to half of that.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling the CDs to sterilize the inflows, first responded to what it called speculative attacks by increasing its open market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 It purchased $3.27 billion in January, including a single-day record $437.7 million on Jan. 14.   \par \par \uc2 In all of 2007, \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  totaled $10.31 billion.   \par \par \uc2 Responds With New Measures   \par \par \uc2 Reluctant to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  indefinitely, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  then responded by with a series of measures, including some to reduce the ease with which investors could dispose of sol-denominated instruments.   \par \par \uc2 From Monday, for example, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started to sell non-negotiable certificates of deposit.   \par \par \uc2 On Monday, it placed a series of the non-negotiable CDs, totaling more than $900 million, and followed it up on Tuesday by placing about $1.0 billion worth of the short-term sol-denominated CDs.   \par \par \uc2 It has also lifted the reserve requirements that banks have with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , called the encaje.   \par \par \uc2 "This increase in the encaje for the local and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced liquidity in the market, a measure that also had the advantage of not attracting speculative funds and was the equivalent of a 50 basis point increase in the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reference rate," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.   \par \par \uc2 With the new measures taking effect, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Jan. 30, when it purchased $249 million.   \par \par \uc2 The sol, meanwhile, has continued to strengthen slightly in recent trading sessions, ending Wednesday at a midrate of PEN2.9165 to the U.S. dollar.   \par \par \uc2 (Robert Kozak is Peru bureau chief for Dow Jones Newswires)   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511 221 7050; peru@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 06-02-08 201