\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes End Lower; Sol Weakens   \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2008\par 22:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended slightly lower Thursday, dragged down by weakness on Wall Street.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index fell 51.83 points, or 0.35%, to end at 14,795.86. The selective blue-chip index fell 37.21 points, or 0.16%, to finish at 23,412.50.   \par \par \uc2 By end of trading on Wednesday, the general index had fallen 15% so far this year.   \par \par \uc2 The Dow Jones Industrial Average dropped more than 300 points Thursday, to close at 12,159.   \par \par \uc2 On Thursday,  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) fell 5.8% to end at $83.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) lost 2.6% to end at $75.50.   \par \par \uc2 Telefonica SA\uc2  (TEF) declined 1.4% to end at $93.65, following the direction of its New York-traded American Depositary Receipt.   \par \par \uc2 In a report, Banco de Credito said stock market investors will be closely watching fourth-quarter financial results. It said that slightly lower metals prices will have affected mining companies, while those companies tied to domestic demand sectors will present solid results.   \par \par \uc2 "For 2008 we expect that corporate profits will continue growing, although at a slower rate than in the last two years," it added.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended weaker at a midrate of PEN2.9540 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9530-PEN2.9550.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN2.9515 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9500-PEN2.9530.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $32 million.   \par \par \uc2 So far this year the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase $2.36 billion.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 01-17-08 1624ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020080117e41h0007u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
