\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes Tumble, End Lower; Sol Weakens   \b0\par\par\uc2 360 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2008\par 22:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes continued to tumble Wednesday, ending sharply lower as declining mineral dragged down many mining company shares.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index decreased 843.45 points, or 5.38%, to end at 14,847.69.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index fell 1,555.45 points, or 6.22%, to finish at 23,449.71.   \par \par \uc2 "What is happening is that some markets are more volatile than others. When things are going well the Lima exchange rises sharply, but when there is a lot of nervousness it can fall a lot," said one market analyst.   \par \par \uc2 The general index is now well down from its July 9, 2007 high of 23,073.84, while the selective index is down from its high of 40,476.10 on the same day.   \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday,  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) fell 6.3% to end at $88.10 on weaker copper prices. Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) lost 6.1% at end at $23.99.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) fell 1.3% to end at $77.50.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly weaker at a midrate of PEN2.9515 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9500-PEN2.9530.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN2.9435 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9430-PEN2.9440.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Wednesday after purchasing $478.7 million in the previous session, which was a single-day record high.   \par \par \uc2 There has been strong demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from foreign and local investors.   \par \par \uc2 Central Reserve Bank of Peru President Julio Velarde had said Wednesday in a radio interview that speculation was driving a recent burst of buying of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 He added the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had the capacity to handle the ongoing volatility and would take measures to cut into the profitability of speculating.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 01-16-08 1625ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020080116e41g000am\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
