\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  VIEW: Peru Sol's Strength Shows No Sign Of Waning   \b0\par\par\uc2 880 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2008\par 22:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 By Robert Kozak   \par \par \uc2 A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's fiery sol should continue to appreciate against the U.S. dollar, fueled by a red-hot economic performance, rising interest rates and robust inflows of cash.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which appreciated some 7.0% against the dollar in 2007 and 6.4% in 2006, has drawn intense interest, especially from foreign investors. It's up 1.4% so far this month, and closed Monday at PEN2.9435 a dollar.   \par \par \uc2 In a bid to slow its gains, the Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sharply stepped up its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 "Beyond any volatility that could be triggered by core market jitters at some point, the appreciation bias of the sol is unlikely to wane this year,"  \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  said in a recent report.   \par \par \uc2 The investment bank said the sol's gains were due to a combination of strong growth in gross domestic product - expected to have expanded 8.3% last year - persistently high commodity prices, a trade surplus still near the highs for the decade, solid foreign direct investment flows and the continuing de-dollarization of domestic portfolios.   \par \par \uc2 Over the last few years, a gradual process of greater use of the sol has taken place, particularly in bank loans.   \par \par \uc2 It forecast a level of PEN2.85 to the dollar at the end of 2008, although that spot level could be reached during the first half of the year, it added.   \par \par \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  said it is also bullish on the dollar/sol rate and expects it to "grind lower towards 2.85 (a 2.5% decline from 2.9225 on the Jan. 11 close) over the next couple of months."   \par \par \uc2 In a recent report, it pointed to the widening interest rate spread between Peru and the U.S. as a reason for the sol's strength against the U.S. unit. Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  lifted its reference rate 25 basis points to 5.25% last week, due to concerns about increased inflationary expectations tied in good part to imported food prices.   \par \par \uc2 Some forecasters are saying the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could continue to tighten monetary policy this year, perhaps lifting the reference rate to as high as 6.0%.   \par \par \uc2 That comes about at a time when expectations are high for an easing of monetary policy in the U.S.   \par \par \uc2 Economists also point to the continuing de-dollarization of the economy. Both dollars and soles are widely used, but the sol is clearly becoming a more favored \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 They also point to the likelihood of continued strong foreign direct investment, tied to a recently signed free trade agreement with the U.S. and an expected near-term jump in Peru's credit rating to investment grade.   \par \par \uc2 Strong remittances by Peruvians living abroad have also supported the sol.   \par \par \uc2 How Long Will \b \highlight22\uc2 Interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  Last?   \par \par \uc2 Economists wonder how long the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be willing to assume the cost of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased some $10.3 billion last year, aiming to smooth out movements in the market and to avoid undermining the competitiveness of Peru's non-commodity exports, analysts say.   \par \par \uc2 Just in the last five trading sessions, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to purchase some $1.68 billion.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchased a record one-day amount of $437.7 million on Monday - in a spot market that  \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  estimates normally has average daily volume of around $300 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  have driven \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign reserves to a record high $28.31 billion as of Jan. 7.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sterilizes those inflows by issuing certificates of deposit.   \par \par \uc2 "While the BCRP will likely maintain its \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases to smooth volatility, the increasing cost of sterilization may limit the room to sustain more \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation,"  \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2  said.   \par \par \uc2 It added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could lean toward accepting greater sol appreciation as a way to ease rising inflation pressures.   \par \par \uc2 The consumer price index for Lima rose 3.93% in 2007, above the upper range of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target range of 1.0% to 3.0%.   \par \par \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  said in a recent report that, "In our view the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not too concerned about the cost of sterilizing its purchases and, like other banks in the region, it may be willing to temporarily have a quasi-fiscal deficit."   \par \par \uc2 It estimated that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still managed to post a small quasi-fiscal surplus last year, despite the sizable dollar purchases.   \par \par \uc2 "We think that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue with its current policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. It won't let the exchange rate appreciate rapidly but will maintain the trend throughout the year," Scotiabank said in a report.   \par \par \uc2 (Robert Kozak is Dow Jones Newswires' Peru bureau chief)   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 511-221-7050; peru@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 14-01-08 2127GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080114e41e0010r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
