\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Peru Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\uc2  To Buy $437.7 Million-Official   \b0\par\par\uc2 132 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2008\par 19:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $437.7 million, a single-day record high amount, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said.   \par \par \uc2 That follows \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of $347 million on Friday of last week, $363 million Thursday, $306 million Wednesday and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of $231 million Tuesday.   \par \par \uc2 There has been strong demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from foreign investors, some of whom are investing in \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  certificates of deposit, market analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended unchanged at a midrate of PEN2.9435 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN2.9430-PEN2.9440.   \par \par \uc2 -Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    \par -0- \par     \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 14-01-08 1841GMT ]   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080114e41e000z6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
