\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Stock Indexes Continue To Decline; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 361 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2008\par 22:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended lower Friday, dragged down by weakness on Wall Street.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index decreased 358.86 points, or 2.13%, to end at 16,486.69.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index fell 843.05 points, or 3.07%, to finish at 26,613.82.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2 (PCU) fell 2.0% to end at $96.00, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) decreased 1.1% at end at $26.40.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) lost 4.6% to end at 7.03 soles ($2.38) as zinc prices eased.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly stronger at a midrate of PEN2.9435 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9430-PEN2.9440.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN2.9595 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9590-PEN2.9600.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $347 million.   \par \par \uc2 There has been strong demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from foreign investors, many of whom are investing in \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  certificates of deposit, market analysts said.   \par \par \uc2 "Expectations of an appreciation of the sol continue as a consequence of the increase in the reference rate to 5.2% from 5.0% and an expected 50 basis point reduction in the reference rate of the U.S. Federal Reserve," consulting firm Macroconsult said in a report.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of Peru late Thursday increased its reference rate by 25 basis points to 5.25%.   \par \par \uc2 "Given prospects that the Peru-U.S. interest rate differential will widen over the next few months as the Fed eases and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Peru either remains on hold or possibly hikes, we believe the PEN is likely to remain well bid and may appreciate beyond our current 12-month forecast of PEN2.92 per dollar,"  \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  said in a report.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 01-11-08 1630ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020080111e41b0007j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
