\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Weaker; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2008\par 22:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended lower Thursday as metals prices again declined, which in turn weakened mining companies.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index decreased 276.68 points, or 1.62%, to end at 16,845.55.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index fell 685.79 points, or 2.44%, to finish at 27,456.87.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) decreased 0.4% at end at $26.70 on weaker copper prices.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) lost 4.3% to end at 7.37 soles ($2.49) as zinc prices eased.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) fell 0.3% to end at $76.10.   \par \par \uc2 Banco de Credito said in a report that "local investors have been taking profits in line with increased expectations of a recession in the United States that could affect emerging economies and demand for commodities."   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly stronger at a midrate of PEN2.9595 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9590-PEN2.9600.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN2.9615 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9610-PEN2.9620.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $363 million.   \par \par \uc2 That was a record amount for a single day \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and follows \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of $306 million Wednesday and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of $231 million