\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Lower; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 349 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2007\par 22:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended lower Monday, dragged down by a decline in mineral prices that weakened mining companies.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index fell 74.89 points, or 0.39%, to end at 19,062.71.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index decreased 158.92 points, or 0.49%, to finish at 32,284.80.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) decreased 3.5% at end at $30.10, while  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) fell 1.5% to end at $116.25, on weaker copper prices.   \par \par \uc2 Base metals miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) lost 1.0% to end at 9.60 soles ($3.20) as zinc prices eased.   \par \par \uc2 Going the other way was financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP), which rose 3.4% to end at $76.   \par \par \uc2 "Despite the fact that the fundamentals of the Peruvian economy remain solid, the development of the Peruvian stock market continues to depend mainly on the international financial climate and movements in metal prices," Scotiabank said in a report.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $1 million.   \par \par \uc2 That follows a one-day record \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of $299 million on Friday, when strong demand for soles from foreign investors placed appreciation pressures on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended Monday stronger at a midrate of PEN2.9725 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9720-PEN2.9730.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN2.9815 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9810-PEN2.9820.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say that the sol is expected to strengthen in coming days due to an upcoming tax payment period and the need for companies to obtain soles to pay end-of-year bonuses.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 12-10-07 1629ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020071210e3ca0007v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
