\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Strengthens A Bit   \b0\par\par\uc2 257 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2007\par 21:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes increased Thursday, lifted by stronger metal prices that benefited mining companies.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index rose 549.85 points, or 3.24%, to end at 17,505.33.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index increased 986.07 points, or 3.47%, to finish at 29,393.61.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miners were lifted by a rise in the price for the metal.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) increased 2.5% to end at $104.00, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA(CVERDEC1.VL) gained 4.8% to end at $26.00.   \par \par \uc2 Base metals miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) increased 3.1% to end at 10.00 soles ($3.33) as zinc prices rose.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) also rose, gaining 1.9% to end at $70.00.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly stronger at a midrate of PEN3.0025 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.0010-PEN3.0040.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN3.0035 to the dollar on a spread of PEN3.0030-PEN3.0040.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday.   \par \par \uc2 In a report, Banco de Credito said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  actively in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 