\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes Tumble Sharply; Sol Weakens   \b0\par\par\uc2 437 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2007\par 22:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes tumbled sharply Monday, dragged down by a sharp drop on Wall Street and by lower metals prices.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index fell 1,013.30 points, or 5.27%, to end at 18,197.10.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index decreased 1,981.26 points, or 6.02%, to finish at 30,947.10.   \par \par \uc2 Both indexes are now off record highs reached in early July, when the general index rose to 23,073.84 and the selective index reached 40,476.10.   \par \par \uc2 "In the short term the movements in the stock market will depend on the trend in metals prices, and the publication of new indicators that show the effects of the crisis in the mortgage sector in the United States on other sectors of the economy," Scotiabank said.   \par \par \uc2 On Monday, mining companies were hit especially hard by a decline in both base and precious metals prices.   \par \par \uc2 Miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) dropped 5.0% to end at 157.40 soles ($52.47).   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) fell 6.2% to end at $102.50 on declining copper prices, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) shed 5.7% at end at $26.60.   \par \par \uc2 Tin miner Minsur SAA (MINSURI1.VL) lost 7.7% to end at 8.40 soles, ($3.03) on a decline in tin prices.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc and lead miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) lost 7.5% to end at PEN10.93 as zinc prices eased.   \par \par \uc2 Bucking the trend was financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP), which rose 0.5% to end at $70.00.   \par \par \uc2 Moody's Investors Service on Monday said that robust loan growth and improving financial fundamentals are underpinning a stable outlook for Peru's banking system and deposit ratings.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly weaker at a midrate of PEN2.9990 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN2.9980-PEN3.0000.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN2.9980 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9970-PEN2.9990.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $1 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say that demand for the sol should remain steady in coming days as companies seek soles for tax-payment purposes.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 11-19-07 1629ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020071119e3bj00075\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
