\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 260 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2007\par 22:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended sharply higher Wednesday, lifted by rising metal prices, especially for copper.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index rose 419.54 points, or 2.16%, to end at 19,835.00.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index advanced 893.62 points, or 2.69%, to finish at 34,152.50.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) rose 2.7% to end at $114.00 on stronger copper prices, while copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA (CVERDEC1.VL) gained 7.6% to $29.60.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) rose 1.2% to $71.15.   \par \par \uc2 Precious metals miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) gained 2.4% to 172.00 soles ($57.33) as gold prices rose.   \par \par \uc2 Citi Investment Research in a report raised its mid-2008 target on the general index to 25,000, up from 24,000 previously.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $10 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly stronger at a midrate of PEN2.9950 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9940-PEN2.9960.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN2.9975 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9970-PEN2.9980.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221-7050; pe