\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Slightly Lower; Sol Weakens   \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2007\par 22:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended slightly weaker Tuesday, pulled down by weakness in a number of smaller shares.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index fell 26.71 points, or 0.14%, to end at 19,415.46.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index decreased 136.76 points, or 0.41%, to finish at 33,258.88.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) lost 0.6% to end at 12.08 soles ($4.03) in heavy trade.   \par \par \uc2 Zinc-lead miner  \uc2 Compania Minera Atacocha SA\uc2  (ATACOC1.VL) fell 0.1% to end at PEN7.89, also in heavy trade.   \par \par \uc2 Going the other way was  \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU), which rose 7.5% to end at $110.00. Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) rose 5.7% to end at $70.30.   \par \par \uc2 Citi Investment Research on Tuesday upgraded Peruvian stocks to overweight from neutral on recent share underperformance and solid macroeconomic fundamentals.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $165 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly weaker Tuesday at a midrate of PEN2.9975 to the U.S. dollar on a spread of PEN2.9970-PEN2.9980.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN2.9935 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9930-PEN2.9940.   \par \par \uc2 Brokerage Centura on Tuesday said that it has revised its forecast for the year-end exchange rate to PEN2.996 per dollar from its previous forecast of PEN3.150 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 -Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 11-13-07 1638ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020071113e3bd00087\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
