\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Sharply Lower; Sol Strengthens   \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2007\par 22:48\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended sharply lower Monday, driven down by weaker prices for precious and base metals.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index fell 355.63 points, or 1.80%, to end at 19,442.17.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index declined 618.73 points, or 1.82%, to finish at 33,395.64.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) dropped 9.8% to end at $103.25.   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA(CVERDEC1.VL) slid 4.2% to $27.39 in heavy trading.   \par \par \uc2 Miner  \uc2 Compania de Minas Buenaventura\uc2  SAA (BVN) tumbled 6.4% to 168.00 soles ($56.00) on weaker gold and copper prices.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) fell 2.2% to end at $66.50.   \par \par \uc2 Pointing to global stock markets, Scotiabank said in a report that "If the nervousness continues, then it is probable that profit-taking will continue on the (Lima) stock market."   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Monday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $14 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended slightly stronger at a midrate of PEN2.9935 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9930-PEN2.9940.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN2.9945 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9940-PEN2.9950.   \par \par \uc2 Consulting company Macroconsult said in a report that the sol is expected to remain strong due to a tax payment period, which should lead to an increase in demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the corporate sector.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 11-12-07 1648ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020071112e3bc0007n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
