\par\par \b \uc2 Peru's Main Stock Indexes End Higher; Sol Strengthens Again   \b0\par\par\uc2 325 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2007\par 22:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2007 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 LIMA (Dow Jones)--Peru's main stock indexes ended higher Friday, as strength in some blue chip shares helped lift the overall stock market.   \par \par \uc2 According to preliminary results, the Lima Stock Exchange's general index rose 107.84 points, or 0.55%, to end at 19,787.80.   \par \par \uc2 The selective blue-chip index increased 296.03 points, or 0.88%, to finish at 34,014.37.   \par \par \uc2 In a radio interview Friday former Finance Minister Pedro Pablo Kuczynski said that room for more gains on the stock market this year may be limited, "and in the coming year it will likely be less buoyant."   \par \par \uc2 Up to Thursday the general index had risen some 53% during the year.   \par \par \uc2 On Friday, zinc miner Compania Minera Volcan SAA (VOLB.VL) rose 2.2% to end at 12.50 soles. ($4.17)   \par \par \uc2 Copper miner Sociedad Minera Cerro Verde SAA(CVERDEC1.VL) increased 0.4% at end at $28.60 in heavy trade.   \par \par \uc2 Southern Copper Corp.\uc2  (PCU) went the other way, dropping 5.7% to end at $114.45.   \par \par \uc2 Financial holding company  \uc2 Credicorp Ltd.\uc2  (BAP) fell 4.6% to end at $68.00.   \par \par \uc2 The Central Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Peru intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to purchase $135 million.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to smooth out movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and to build foreign reserves.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended at a midrate of PEN2.9945 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9940-PEN2.9950.   \par \par \uc2 The sol ended the previous session at a midrate of PEN2.9990 to the dollar on a spread of PEN2.9980-PEN3.0000.   \par \par \uc2 A market analyst said strong demand for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was tied to approval by the U.S. House of Representatives on Thursday of a free trade deal with Peru.   \par \par \uc2 -By Robert Kozak, Dow Jones Newswires; 51-1-221 7050; peru@dowjones.com [ 11-09-07 1634ET ]   \par \par \uc2 1071 1837   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020071109e3b9000aw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
